{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_01MCvwp243HYtwgvDTbJf797","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. **Q18: Stateless vs stateful agents?** is written and committed.\n\nThe note covers:\n\n- **Concept** — stateless = full history in prompt every call; stateful = external checkpoint (Redis/Postgres) loaded selectively per turn\n- **Mechanism** — LangGraph `PostgresSaver` checkpointer with `thread_id` for crash-resume; selective loading (last-N turns + rolling summary) vs full-history injection\n- **Cost math** — 1K concurrent sessions × 10 turns × 8K tokens = 80M tokens/day stateless → ~20M stateful (75% reduction)\n- **Heuristic** — stateless for tasks under 5 turns / 30 seconds; stateful for longer tasks, regulated domains, or anything needing crash recovery\n- **Three pitfalls** — \"stateful always wins\" (wrong), \"just store full history in DB\" (misses selective loading), ignoring crash recovery as the key stateful benefit\n\nNext up: **Q19 — Version and roll back agent behavior.**"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":344,"cache_read_input_tokens":63086,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":344,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"822bff9a-6011-42d5-a1e9-0153b3eb6636","uuid":"b77dcf6f-72e8-4cf2-ae40-aec3e80f4813"}
